  "ticket_id": "2c28-e5b9",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "Four new ticket CLI subcommands exist and are callable via the ticket CLI dispatcher: next-batch (batch selection with hierarchy walk, blocking checks, file-overlap serialization, greedy selection \u2014 replaces sprint-next-batch.sh/issue-batch.sh; preserves SKIPPED_DESIGN_AWAITING, SKIPPED_BLOCKED_STORY, SKIPPED_NEEDS_PLANNING output tokens and --json format consumed by write-blackboard.sh), list-descendants (BFS tree walk returning child IDs by tier as a JSON object keyed by tier name), list-epics (epic listing with blocking status, child counts, priority sorting \u2014 replaces sprint-list-epics.sh; preserves tab-separated output format with blocker_ids field), and exists (O(1) ticket existence check via directory + CREATE-file presence without invoking the reducer \u2014 replaces direct filesystem checks in pre-commit-ticket-gate.sh)",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capability (four CLI subcommands are available and callable) phrased as ongoing behavior, though the detailed replacement context adds minor ambiguity about whether focus is on the end-state capability or task completion"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Each new subcommand has an integration test in tests/ that exercises the subcommand through the ticket CLI dispatcher against a synthetic .tickets-tracker/ fixture directory (following the existing pattern in test-sprint-next-batch.sh). Output equivalence means: same exit code contract (0=success, non-zero=failure; validate's 5-tier scored exit codes 0-4 are preserved where applicable), same top-level JSON keys and value correctness when output is structured, and same human-readable summary format when output is plain text. For next-batch specifically, tests assert correct blocking behavior (blocked story's child tasks excluded from batch) and correct file-overlap serialization (overlapping files produce exactly one SKIPPED_OVERLAP)",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system property (integration tests exist and follow a pattern) that remains true after implementation, phrased as an ongoing behavioral capability"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A script author can retrieve next-batch, list-descendants, list-epics, and exists results using only ticket CLI commands \u2014 no knowledge of .tickets-tracker/ directory layout required \u2014 verified by integration tests exercising each subcommand end-to-end through the CLI dispatcher",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable capability of the system (script authors can retrieve results via CLI) that persists after the work is complete, verified by ongoing integration tests"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
